++   The shell selector is not redundant: styles.css carries an AA override block on
++   `.v8-product-shell` (--v8-muted / -amber / -coral) that this file has always beaten
++   by load order at equal specificity.  Binding :root alone would let that override
++   win again inside the shell, silently resurrecting declarations that were dead
++   code.  Keeping both selectors preserves the shell's effective values exactly while
++   extending them to the screen that has no shell. */
++:root,
